{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>And a knob under the two branches.</b> From within the knob the branches were drawn out from its two sides, this way and that. Thus we learned in the work of the Tabernacle: The height of the menorah was eighteen handbreadths. The legs and the flower — three handbreadths; this is the flower mentioned in connection with the base, as it says ״עַד יְרֵכָהּ עַד פִּרְחָהּ״ (Numbers 8). And two handbreadths smooth. And one handbreadth in which was a bowl — from the four bowls, and knob and flower, of the two knobs and two flowers mentioned in the menorah itself, as it says ״מְשֻׁקָּדִים כַּפְתּוֹרֶיהָ וּפְרָחֶיהָ״ — we learn that in the shaft there were two knobs and two flowers, apart from the three knobs from which the branches were drawn, as it says ״וְכַפְתֹּר תַּחַת שְׁנֵי הַקָּנִים״ etc. And two handbreadths smooth. And one handbreadth: knob and two branches coming out of it this way and that, drawn out and rising alongside the height of the menorah. One handbreadth smooth. And one handbreadth: knob and two branches coming out of it. And one handbreadth smooth. And one handbreadth: knob and two branches coming out of it, drawn out and rising alongside the height of the menorah. And two handbreadths smooth. There remained three handbreadths, in which were three bowls and a knob and a flower. So the bowls totaled twenty-two — eighteen for the six branches, three for each one, and four on the body of the menorah itself — that is twenty-two. And eleven knobs: six on the six branches, and three on the body of the menorah from which the branches come out, and two more on the menorah, as it says ״מְשֻׁקָּדִים כַּפְתּוֹרֶיהָ״ — and subtracting two knobs: one below near the base, and one in the upper three handbreadths together with the three bowls. And it had nine flowers: six for the six branches, as it says ״בַּקָּנֶה הָאֶחָד כַּפְתֹּר וָפֶרַח״, and three for the menorah, as it says ״מְשֻׁקָּדִים כַּפְתּוֹרֶיהָ וּפְרָחֶיהָ״ — and subtracting two flowers, and one mentioned in the section Beha'alotekha: ״עַד יְרֵכָהּ עַד פִּרְחָהּ״. And if you examine this mishna written above precisely, you will find them each and every one in its place."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:39.861143628Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}